.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# The farmer's own details. Name, village, land size — this is personal data and
# must never be committed. The old entry said "profile.json"; the file is
# actually called farmer_profile.json, so it was being committed.
farmer_profile.json
profile.json

# Caches that rebuild themselves. Committing them means shipping stale prices
# and somebody else's village.
market_cache.json
places_cache.json

# The local fallback index: a numpy blob plus its metadata. Normally a build
# artifact and normally not committed -- but a deployed Space has no build step
# and its disk is wiped on every sleep, so an uncommitted index means the app
# wakes up empty and answers nothing. It is a couple of MB. Ship it.
# Rebuild with: python ingest.py --recreate
!models/local_kb/
models/*.bin
qdrant_storage/

# Source documents: the curated .md knowledge base is tracked, anything else a
# user drops in is not.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/*.md

# Personal files that drifted into the project root. Not part of the project
# and not something to publish with it.
Expense sheet personal .xlsx
*.xlsx

# Evaluation output IS tracked on purpose -- eval/results.{jsonl,csv} is the
# headline result the README promises, so it must not be ignored here.
